---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
// Source of every statement below: docs/PRIVACY_POLICY_INPUTS.md.
// Items marked "To be confirmed" map to its section 10 open questions.
---
<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How BeyondRep handles your data: what is stored on your phone, what is backed up to your account, how Apple Health and Health Connect data is used, and how to export or delete it."
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your workouts are stored on your phone. Only workouts you finish are backed up to your account.</li>
    <li>We collect your email address so you can sign in. We do not ask for your name, phone number, location or contacts.</li>
    <li>If you connect Apple Health or Health Connect, BeyondRep reads a few values to show you a daily summary. They never leave your phone and are never saved.</li>
    <li>There are no ads, no analytics, no tracking across apps or websites, and we do not sell or share your data.</li>
    <li>You can export your workouts or delete your account at any time from inside the app.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    BeyondRep (app ID <code>{SITE.appId}</code>) is responsible for the personal data described here.
    The legal name and postal country of the data controller are <em>to be confirmed</em>.
    Contact us about privacy at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.privacyEmail}`}>{SITE.privacyEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
  <h3>Your account</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Email address</td><td>To create your account and send you one-time sign-in codes. Never used for marketing.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Account ID (a random identifier)</td><td>To tie your backed-up workouts to your account.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>One-time sign-in codes</td><td>To confirm it’s you. Stored only in hashed form by our authentication provider and valid for 10 minutes.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Session tokens</td><td>To keep you signed in securely. Kept in your phone’s secure storage (Keychain on iOS, Keystore on Android).</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sign-in times, IP address and device type of sign-in requests</td><td>Recorded by our authentication provider to keep accounts secure and prevent abuse.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Workouts you finish</h3>
  <p>
    When you finish a workout, BeyondRep backs it up so you can restore it on another phone. A backed-up workout contains
    its name, start and finish times, your time zone offset, and each exercise (name, muscle group, equipment) and set
    (type, reps, weight, unit, RPE, completion time). We also keep totals such as working sets and volume, and a short
    record that a workout was deleted so your other phones remove it too.
  </p>
  <p>
    Workout and exercise names are free text. Please don’t put sensitive information in them.
  </p>
  <p>
    To stop the same upload being saved twice, we keep a receipt of each upload for 90 days. It contains identifiers and a
    one-way hash of the upload, not the workout itself.
  </p>

  <h3>What is never backed up</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Workouts in progress, paused or discarded, and rest-timer state</li>
    <li>Your plans, templates and their notes, and custom exercises in the catalog</li>
    <li>Any Apple Health or Health Connect data</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These stay on your phone. Your phone’s local BeyondRep data is excluded from iCloud, iTunes and Android backups.</p>

  <h2>Apple Health and Health Connect</h2>
  <p>
    Connecting is optional and only happens when you tap Connect. BeyondRep then asks your phone for permission to read
    last night’s sleep, today’s steps, your most recent resting heart rate (last 7 days) and your most recent weight
    (last 30 days). It does not write or change anything in Apple Health or Health Connect.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>These values are used only to show you a daily summary in the app.</li>
    <li>They are held in memory while the app is open. They are never written to disk, backed up to your account, included in exports, logged or sent to anyone.</li>
    <li>The only thing stored is a note that you connected, which is removed when you disconnect or delete your account.</li>
    <li>Health data is never used for advertising, marketing or data mining, and is never sold or shared.</li>
    <li>To stop access, tap Disconnect in the app and revoke access in the Health app (iOS) or Health Connect settings (Android).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    BeyondRep’s use of information received from Health Connect follows the Health Connect Permissions policy, including
    the Limited Use requirements. The daily summary is for your information only. It is not medical advice or a diagnosis.
  </p>

  <h2>Service providers</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>What it does</th><th>Data it handles</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><a href="https://supabase.com/privacy">Supabase</a></td><td>Sign-in, database and account deletion, hosted in Mumbai, India (AWS ap-south-1)</td><td>Email, account ID, tokens, sign-in IP and device type, finished workouts, upload receipts</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/">Brevo</a></td><td>Sends sign-in code emails</td><td>Email address, the code email, and delivery and open logs</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare</a></td><td>Hosts this website and receives email sent to our addresses</td><td>Website visitors’ IP addresses and browser details in request logs; emails you send us, which it forwards</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Our email mailbox provider (<em>to be confirmed</em>)</td><td>Stores emails you send us and our replies</td><td>Your email address and what you write to us</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Apple and Google</td><td>App distribution, and Apple Health or Health Connect on your phone</td><td>Handled under their own privacy policies. Health data stays on your phone.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>These providers act on our behalf. We do not sell or share your personal data with anyone else.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Kept until</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Finished workouts</td><td>You delete the workout or your account</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Records of deleted workouts</td><td>You delete your account</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Upload receipts</td><td>90 days, removed daily after that</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Account, sessions and tokens</td><td>You delete your account</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Security logs held by our authentication provider (these include your email address and IP address), and Brevo’s delivery logs and contact record</td><td><em>To be confirmed</em></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Database backups held by our hosting provider</td><td>Until they roll off the provider’s backup window (period <em>to be confirmed</em>)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Data on your phone</td><td>You delete your account or uninstall the app. On iOS, the sign-in token in the Keychain can survive an uninstall.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Apple Health and Health Connect values</td><td>Not kept</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>This website and emails you send us</h2>
  <p>
    This website uses no cookies, analytics or tracking. Our host, Cloudflare, processes visitors’ IP addresses and browser
    details to serve pages and protect against abuse.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you email us, including to ask to be told when BeyondRep launches, we use your address only to reply or send that
    one launch email. Launch-notification addresses are deleted after the launch email is sent, or sooner if you ask.
  </p>

  <h2>Where data is processed</h2>
  <p>
    Account and workout data is stored in India. Our email provider, Brevo, is based in the European Union. Which other
    countries’ rules apply is <em>to be confirmed</em>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Get a copy:</strong> In Account, <strong>Export cloud workout history (JSON)</strong> saves your backed-up workouts as a JSON file to a place you choose.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete a workout:</strong> open it from history and tap Delete workout. It is removed from your backup too.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete your account:</strong> see <a href="/delete-account">Delete your account</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw health access:</strong> Disconnect in the app, then revoke access in your phone’s health settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Ask a question or complain:</strong> email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.privacyEmail}`}>{SITE.privacyEmail}</a>. You can also contact your local data protection authority.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Data travels over encrypted HTTPS connections. Each account can only read its own workouts, enforced by the database.
    Sign-in tokens are kept in your phone’s secure storage, and server keys never ship in the app.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>BeyondRep is not intended for children. The minimum age is <em>to be confirmed</em>.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how BeyondRep handles your data, we will update this page and its date first, and tell you in the app
    or by email before a significant change takes effect.
  </p>
</Legal>
